WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:01.440
- When I ride,

00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:04.080
it just feels like
everything else washes away.

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:04.913
(bike engine roars)

00:00:04.913 --> 00:00:05.810
Nothing is important

00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:08.290
other than what I'm doing right there.

00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:09.410
That's just the best feeling ever,

00:00:09.410 --> 00:00:11.653
that feeling of freedom from everything.

00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:16.677
(calm music)

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:19.610
- My name is Mark Beaumont,

00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:21.010
and I'm an endurance athlete.

00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:25.010
With the current world record
for cycling around the planet,

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:28.770
seeking adventures and finding stories

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:31.010
is what I'm most passionate about.

00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:32.460
Ever since I can remember,

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:35.063
I've had that sense of
curiosity about the world.

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:39.123
This time I've come to Dubai.

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:44.720
I'm going to meet Dana,

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:47.160
a bike rider who's been
inspiring young girls

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:48.343
all over the UAE.

00:00:49.775 --> 00:00:52.525
(powerful music)

00:00:53.390 --> 00:00:55.360
- I was born and raised in Dubai.

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:57.460
So I've lived here for 25 years.

00:00:57.460 --> 00:01:00.680
I've been riding dirt bikes since I'm 15.

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:03.500
Growing up here, my dad
always taught me how

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:06.480
to do pretty much any
sport that I wanted to do.

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:09.190
I grew up learning how to
wakeboard, to drive my new car,

00:01:09.190 --> 00:01:10.023
things like that.

00:01:10.023 --> 00:01:11.380
I never felt like there was anything

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:12.940
I couldn't do just because I'm a girl.

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:14.150
If there's a sport that I wanna learn,

00:01:14.150 --> 00:01:14.983
yeah, let's go for it.

00:01:14.983 --> 00:01:16.360
There's nothing holding me back.

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:18.930
When I started riding,
it just felt natural

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:20.440
to do that as well.

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:22.590
I just loved it from the very beginning.

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:25.430
So I started racing in the
Emirates Desert Championship.

00:01:25.430 --> 00:01:27.470
And that's a two hour race,

00:01:27.470 --> 00:01:29.630
around like a 20 to 25 kilometer loop.

00:01:29.630 --> 00:01:31.220
And I was doing a couple of those,

00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:34.150
and then I started riding a
bit on the motocross track.

00:01:34.150 --> 00:01:35.960
And they really wanted
more girls to be racing

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:38.260
so I did a couple of motocross races,

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:40.210
and then I did one rally,

00:01:40.210 --> 00:01:41.890
which was the Dubai International Rally.

00:01:41.890 --> 00:01:45.300
And that was probably
my favorite race ever.

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:47.050
So, let me show you the bikes
that we're gonna ride today.

00:01:47.050 --> 00:01:48.500
- [Mark] This is pretty cool.

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:49.333
- Yeah.

00:01:49.333 --> 00:01:51.222
- I'm not used to having
an engine on my bike.

00:01:51.222 --> 00:01:52.178
(laughing)

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:54.170
- So these are the two
bikes we're gonna take out.

00:01:54.170 --> 00:01:56.830
We've got the 450-SXF, the 350-SXF.

00:01:56.830 --> 00:01:58.560
- I guess they're the same size of bike,

00:01:58.560 --> 00:01:59.450
it's just a bigger engine.

00:01:59.450 --> 00:02:00.640
- Exactly, yeah.

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:01.473
- And what's the idea?

00:02:01.473 --> 00:02:02.880
We're gonna go out there, and you're gonna

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:03.820
show me the basics?

00:02:03.820 --> 00:02:06.640
- Yeah, so we'll maybe
just start on a flat area.

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:08.050
And I'll show you as well, like,

00:02:08.050 --> 00:02:09.740
what kind of lines you
wanna take in the dunes

00:02:09.740 --> 00:02:12.200
'cause you don't really
wanna just go straight over

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:13.430
'cause that's quite rough on you.

00:02:13.430 --> 00:02:15.230
But yeah let's get you kitted up,

00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:16.063
get the bikes up,

00:02:16.063 --> 00:02:17.540
and let's head into the desert.

00:02:20.007 --> 00:02:22.890
(soft music)

00:02:22.890 --> 00:02:24.710
- Because it's such a
melting pot of cultures,

00:02:24.710 --> 00:02:26.600
how would you reflect growing up here?

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:28.940
- Yeah, I mean having
an international culture

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:31.500
around you is my normal.

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:33.250
It feels odd not to have that.

00:02:33.250 --> 00:02:35.930
And yeah, you get to learn
so many different cultures,

00:02:35.930 --> 00:02:38.814
traditions, how people
tick, how they work.

00:02:38.814 --> 00:02:41.231
(soft music)

00:02:48.920 --> 00:02:50.670
When I tell people about
riding in the desert,

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:53.670
I describe it kind of
as surfing in the dunes.

00:02:53.670 --> 00:02:55.070
It's like you're cutting through butter,

00:02:55.070 --> 00:02:55.903
cutting through water.

00:02:55.903 --> 00:02:57.542
It just feels so natural.

00:02:57.542 --> 00:02:59.300
(bike revving)

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:01.580
It really does like you're
just painting a canvas,

00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:04.080
and you find your lines and
when you find that good line,

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:06.410
it just feels like poetry in motion,

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:07.640
like you're surfing dunes.

00:03:07.640 --> 00:03:09.316
It's just perfect.

00:03:09.316 --> 00:03:13.040
(soft upbeat music)

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:15.500
The riding community here is
just so open and welcoming.

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:16.410
And maybe it is because I'm a girl

00:03:16.410 --> 00:03:17.960
that they're actually more helpful.

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:19.910
There's so many different nationalities,

00:03:19.910 --> 00:03:21.760
you never feel like you don't belong.

00:03:22.757 --> 00:03:27.757
(bike engines growling)
(soft upbeat music)

00:03:43.523 --> 00:03:44.356
Whoo!

00:03:45.236 --> 00:03:46.371
Nice job, dude!

00:03:46.371 --> 00:03:47.311
- Wow!

00:03:47.311 --> 00:03:48.164
- How you feeling?

00:03:48.164 --> 00:03:50.487
- Well, it's a mixture between
sort of laughing and terror.

00:03:50.487 --> 00:03:51.720
(laughing)

00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:53.000
- [Dana] Well, you look
a lot more comfortable

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:54.050
than just a few minutes ago.

00:03:54.050 --> 00:03:56.230
- Yeah, I mean it's child-like, isn't it?

00:03:56.230 --> 00:03:57.710
It's just that sheer glee.

00:03:57.710 --> 00:03:58.990
- Yeah.
- Why did you keep going?

00:03:58.990 --> 00:04:00.500
I mean, so many people
would start something,

00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:01.951
and then when it's up to them,

00:04:01.951 --> 00:04:03.280
they do something else,

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:06.050
but you took it to the next level.

00:04:06.050 --> 00:04:07.850
- Yeah, I kept going 'cause, I mean,

00:04:07.850 --> 00:04:10.710
for me, it was something
that really changed my life

00:04:10.710 --> 00:04:11.750
at the time.

00:04:11.750 --> 00:04:13.560
I was in quite a dark place.

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:15.480
I wasn't confident in myself.

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:18.930
It kind of made me realize how
awesome life actually can be.

00:04:18.930 --> 00:04:21.240
- If the days out on the
bike gave you nothing else,

00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:23.890
that phrase, "It showed
me life could be awesome."

00:04:23.890 --> 00:04:24.723
- [Dana] Yeah. Exactly.

00:04:24.723 --> 00:04:25.556
- That would be enough, wouldn't it?

00:04:25.556 --> 00:04:28.310
- Yeah, no, that's the best
gift I could've asked for.

00:04:28.310 --> 00:04:30.290
I would love to inspire
other girls to ride.

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:33.150
If I could give another girl
that experience that I had,

00:04:33.150 --> 00:04:36.070
and that feeling of
self-confidence, belonging

00:04:36.070 --> 00:04:37.023
that makes my day.

00:04:37.980 --> 00:04:39.490
- [Mark] At the heart of
Dana you've got somebody

00:04:39.490 --> 00:04:40.860
who's very, very sweet and friendly.

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:42.000
And simply wants to show me the bike path,

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:43.850
but a fierce competitor, like I can see

00:04:43.850 --> 00:04:46.390
that undercurrent of, I wanna push this.

00:04:46.390 --> 00:04:48.810
Just trying to keep up
with her around the dunes

00:04:48.810 --> 00:04:50.917
was intimidating enough.

00:04:50.917 --> 00:04:52.080
It was wonderful.

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:53.290
It was eye-opening.

00:04:53.290 --> 00:04:56.492
It was scary but it was seriously cool.

00:04:56.492 --> 00:04:59.075
(serene music)

